  "summary": "Cancellation of sales order {{v1}} is complete and verified. Clicking the form's 'Cancel' button opened a \"Cancel {{v4}}\" confirmation dialog (\"Are you sure you want to cancel this order?\"); I inspected its buttons and clicked the one whose handler is action_cancel (labelled 'Cancel'), which performs the cancellation without sending an email, whereas 'Discard' (special=cancel) only closes the wizard and 'Send and cancel' would also email. (a) The statusbar now displays exactly \"Cancelled\" — it is the current/checked status, and {{v4}} / Quotation Sent / Quotation are now all disabled. (b) The breadcrumb and heading read \"Quotations / {{v1}}\", i.e. the order reference is {{v1}}. Totals after cancelling: Untaxed Amount £6,175.00, TAX 20% £1,235.00, Total £7,410.00. A stacked partner \"Edit: {{v2}}\" modal briefly intercepted the first click; I closed it with its own Discard (no partner data was changed) and the cancellation then applied.",
